[
  {
    "id": "S-1",
    "name": "accounting_policies.md",
    "kind": "document",
    "covers": "The group’s accounting policies",
    "total": { "count": 103, "unit": "lines" },
    "records": ["L26"],
    "excerpt": {
      "type": "text",
      "count": "Showing the Revenue section: 16 of 103 lines",
      "lines": [
        { "n": 12, "text": "## Revenue" },
        { "n": 13, "text": "" },
        { "n": 14, "text": "| Stream | When it is recognised | Account |" },
        { "n": 15, "text": "|---|---|---|" },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "| Equipment (duplicators, printers, drums) | On delivery to the customer. For dealers, on delivery to the dealer | 4000 |"
        },
        { "n": 17, "text": "| Consumables (ink, masters) | On delivery | 4100 |" },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "| Maintenance contracts, annual billing | Billed at the start of the term into contract liabilities (2400). Recognised evenly over the 12 months | 2400 → 4200 |"
        },
        { "n": 19, "text": "| Maintenance contracts, monthly billing | When billed each month | 4200 |" },
        { "n": 20, "text": "| Repair labour and parts | When the work is done or the part delivered | 4200 |" },
        { "n": 21, "text": "| Rental income | Monthly, over the lease | 4300 |" },
        { "n": 22, "text": "| Intercompany sales | Same rules. Eliminated on consolidation | 4500 |" },
        { "n": 23, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 24,
          "text": "- **Revenue excludes consumption tax / VAT / sales tax** (税抜方式). Tax collected is a liability (2300)."
        },
        {
          "n": 25,
          "text": "- **Dealer volume rebates** reduce revenue. They are accrued monthly at 2.5% (KJP), 3% (KUS) or 2% (KDE, KUK) of dealer equipment and consumables sales, and settled quarterly by credit note on the 10th business day after quarter-end, for dealers above the quarterly threshold (¥20m / $120k / €100k / £60k). Accrual not used is released at settlement."
        },
        {
          "n": 26,
          "text": "- **Cut-off:** revenue belongs to the period in which delivery occurs. The `delivery_date` on each invoice is the control field.",
          "cited": true
        },
        { "n": 27, "text": "" }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "S-2",
    "name": "close_calendar.md",
    "kind": "document",
    "covers": "The group’s month-end close, as it stood on 16 Oct 2026",
    "total": { "count": 75, "unit": "lines" },
    "records": [],
    "excerpt": {
      "type": "text",
      "count": "Showing the Where things stand today section: 31 of 75 lines",
      "lines": [
        { "n": 5, "text": "## Where things stand today (Friday 16 October 2026, BD12 of October)" },
        { "n": 6, "text": "" },
        { "n": 7, "text": "| Item | Status |" },
        { "n": 8, "text": "|---|---|" },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "| **September 2026 close** (FY2026-P06, end of H1) | ✅ Closed on **8 Oct (BD6)**. Ledgers locked |"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "| **H1 consolidation** | ✅ Done. Consolidated statements, segments and KPIs published to `05_reporting/` |"
        },
        { "n": 11, "text": "| **FY2026 6+6 forecast** | ✅ Submitted 9 Oct. Version `FC-FY2026-6+6` |" },
        { "n": 12, "text": "| **Q2 dealer rebate credit notes** | ✅ Issued 14 Oct (BD10) |" },
        { "n": 13, "text": "| **October 2026** (FY2026-P07) | 🟡 **Open.** Daily postings through 15 Oct only |" },
        { "n": 14, "text": "| H1 results board meeting | Thu 5 Nov 2026 |" },
        { "n": 15, "text": "| H1 earnings release (決算短信) | Fri 6 Nov 2026, 15:00 JST |" },
        { "n": 16, "text": "| Auditor interim review fieldwork | 19–30 Oct (Marunouchi Audit LLC) |" },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "| KJP interim corporate tax payment | 30 Nov 2026 (H1 tax payable at 30 Sep: ¥0.48bn group) |"
        },
        { "n": 18, "text": "| October close | Target 9 Nov (BD6) |" },
        { "n": 19, "text": "" },
        { "n": 20, "text": "### What October's numbers do and don't contain yet" },
        { "n": 21, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 22,
          "text": "October looks small and odd on any dashboard. **That is expected.** It must be flagged, not compared with full months."
        },
        { "n": 23, "text": "" },
        { "n": 24, "text": "| Already in October | Not in October yet |" },
        { "n": 25, "text": "|---|---|" },
        {
          "n": 26,
          "text": "| Customer invoices and receipts to 15 Oct | Second half of the month's sales and collections |"
        },
        {
          "n": 27,
          "text": "| Supplier invoices received; Friday payment runs (subsidiaries); KJP mid-month run | KJP month-end payment run (30 Oct) |"
        },
        {
          "n": 28,
          "text": "| Intercompany shipments (BD3) | Month-end entries: depreciation, accruals (bonus, warranty, rebates, property tax), deferred revenue release, allowance, FX revaluation, income tax |"
        },
        {
          "n": 29,
          "text": "| US payroll (15 Oct), first half | Japan payroll (23 Oct, as the 25th is a Sunday), UK (28 Oct), Germany/China and US second half (30 Oct) |"
        },
        {
          "n": 30,
          "text": "| Reversal of September's FX revaluation (1 Oct) | Manufacturing month-end variance; production on 16, 23 and 30 Oct |"
        },
        { "n": 31, "text": "| Q2 rebate credit notes | |" },
        { "n": 32, "text": "| Consumption tax / VAT / payroll remittances due in October | |" },
        { "n": 33, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 34,
          "text": "So October currently shows revenue without most of its costs, and receivables with no allowance update."
        },
        { "n": 35, "text": "" }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "S-3",
    "name": "close_memo_2026-09.md",
    "kind": "document",
    "covers": "The controller’s memo on the September 2026 close",
    "total": { "count": 74, "unit": "lines" },
    "records": ["L37-39"],
    "excerpt": {
      "type": "text",
      "count": "Showing the What drove the month section: 24 of 74 lines",
      "lines": [
        { "n": 25, "text": "## What drove the month" },
        { "n": 26, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 27,
          "text": "**1. Sales above budget in local currency in every printing segment.** September is back-to-school month in Europe and the US. In yen, Americas (¥1,064m vs ¥1,089m) and China (¥884m vs ¥892m) came in slightly below budget because of the exchange rate."
        },
        {
          "n": 28,
          "text": "- Japan ¥3,568m external. Equipment was helped by several large dealer orders invoiced in the last days of the month."
        },
        {
          "n": 29,
          "text": "- Europe ¥1,153m. KDE and KUK both had their best month of the year (Sept school restart). Operating margin was 16–17% for the month."
        },
        { "n": 30, "text": "- Americas ¥1,064m. Sales were ahead of budget in dollars." },
        { "n": 31, "text": "- China ¥884m." },
        { "n": 32, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 33,
          "text": "**2. Gross margin 1.2pt below budget.** The stronger yen is the main cause: transfer prices are fixed at budget rates, so goods sold by the subsidiaries earn fewer yen. The plant also had a ¥18m unfavourable variance (material ¥12m, absorption ¥6m). Material variance is now small: pigment prices eased in July and sit below the FY2026 standard, which offsets some material-usage overrun."
        },
        { "n": 34, "text": "" },
        { "n": 35, "text": "**3. Provisions ¥186m vs ¥63m budget.**" },
        { "n": 36, "text": "- **Great Lakes Duplicating Supply (C-KUS-0001)**, US dealer, Michigan." },
        { "n": 37, "text": "  - **Balance:** $1.42m outstanding at 30 Sep vs a $600k credit limit.", "cited": true },
        {
          "n": 38,
          "text": "  - **Payment history:** no payment received since 21 July. $507k is now more than 60 days past due.",
          "cited": true
        },
        {
          "n": 39,
          "text": "  - **Actions:** account on credit hold since 10 Sep. 60% specific reserve booked (prepared by Marcus Bell, approved by Dana Whitfield). KUS allowance up from $173k to $971k.",
          "cited": true
        },
        { "n": 40, "text": "  - **Next step:** legal is reviewing whether to file a claim." },
        { "n": 41, "text": "- The balance is warranty provisions on the higher equipment volume." },
        { "n": 42, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 43,
          "text": "**4. Personnel costs ¥82m under budget.** The hiring freeze has been in place since April. Group headcount was 2,788 at 30 Sep, 47 below March."
        },
        { "n": 44, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 45,
          "text": "**5. Real estate.** Rent was ¥26.0m vs ¥38.6m budget. The 7th floor, vacated by Atago Data Labs on 31 March, is still empty. The budget assumed a new tenant from July."
        },
        { "n": 46, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 47,
          "text": "**6. FX.** The dollar averaged ¥141.2 (budget ¥150.0). KJP booked a ¥32m FX gain in September as the yen weakened slightly from August's ¥139.6."
        },
        { "n": 48, "text": "" }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "S-4",
    "name": "finance_team.md",
    "kind": "document",
    "covers": "Who owns what in finance, and the approval rules",
    "total": { "count": 71, "unit": "lines" },
    "records": ["L68"],
    "excerpt": {
      "type": "text",
      "count": "Showing the Approval rules section: 7 of 71 lines",
      "lines": [
        { "n": 65, "text": "## Approval rules" },
        { "n": 66, "text": "" },
        {
          "n": 67,
          "text": "- **Supplier invoices** are approved by the entity controller. Invoices over 10× the approver's normal limit go to the entity head (CFO for KJP)."
        },
        {
          "n": 68,
          "text": "- **Manual journal entries** must be created by one person and approved by another (**segregation of duties**).",
          "cited": true
        },
        { "n": 69, "text": "- **Write-offs** of receivables need the CFO." },
        {
          "n": 70,
          "text": "- **Intercompany invoices** are auto-approved by the `AUTO-IC` rule when they match a KJP shipment."
        },
        { "n": 71, "text": "- `SYS-ERP` is the system user for automated subledger postings." }
      ]
    }
  },
